WEBVTT

00:07.700 --> 00:10.010
When Hapna hit the market,

00:10.380 --> 00:12.800
it caused quite a stir in the prison too.

00:12.800 --> 00:14.710
The price skyrocketed.

00:15.050 --> 00:17.300
I barely managed to get my hands on some.

00:18.710 --> 00:21.220
Even someone like me, who usually avoids drugs,

00:21.220 --> 00:23.430
swallowed one just for fun

00:23.850 --> 00:26.510
and then immediately headbutted the iron bars.

00:26.640 --> 00:28.220
It hurt like hell.

00:29.220 --> 00:31.610
It seems it had no effect on me at all.

00:32.780 --> 00:34.530
Worse yet,

00:34.730 --> 00:37.030
they said that even if you take it just once,

00:37.030 --> 00:39.230
it becomes toxic in your system.

00:40.160 --> 00:41.910
So now,

00:41.910 --> 00:44.700
I have to track down that old man Skinner.

00:46.330 --> 00:48.700
If I die before finding him,

00:49.200 --> 00:51.550
I'll punch that guy square in the face

00:51.840 --> 00:53.880
in hell.

02:23.680 --> 02:29.390
[LAZARUS]

02:36.560 --> 02:41.030
[Episode 5: Pretty Vacant]

03:04.930 --> 03:08.550
Dr. 909 hacked into Delta Medicinal

03:08.550 --> 03:10.750
and found out that Hapna was dangerous.

03:11.100 --> 03:12.520
The key is

03:12.520 --> 03:16.560
that Delta Medicinal had handled the clinical trials for Hapna.

03:16.560 --> 03:18.190
In other words, they

03:18.190 --> 03:21.030
likely already knew how dangerous Hapna was.

03:21.610 --> 03:23.900
And then, check this video.

03:24.490 --> 03:25.400
Gross.

03:27.030 --> 03:28.900
What is this?

03:29.200 --> 03:31.960
We got this photo from Dr. 909,

03:31.960 --> 03:33.870
but we don't know what it is.

03:33.870 --> 03:36.079
Those guys must have colluded with Skinner

03:36.079 --> 03:38.710
and gotten the permit using fake data, right?

03:38.710 --> 03:40.300
Highly likely.

03:40.590 --> 03:44.050
Anyway, there must be some clues about Skinner there.

03:44.050 --> 03:44.840
Eleina,

03:44.840 --> 03:46.090
how's your side going?

03:46.090 --> 03:47.470
Have you found anything?

03:47.470 --> 03:50.560
I can't find any data that might be related to clinical trials.

03:50.560 --> 03:51.600
But

03:51.600 --> 03:53.390
there's something strange.

03:53.890 --> 03:55.480
Every week, songs are uploaded

03:55.480 --> 03:57.980
from the company server to SoundCloud,

03:57.980 --> 03:59.980
a music-sharing platform.

03:59.980 --> 04:01.860
What's so strange about that?

04:01.860 --> 04:04.820
Perhaps it's just an employee who likes music.

04:04.820 --> 04:05.900
Check this out.

04:19.450 --> 04:20.760
What is this?

04:20.920 --> 04:24.010
This piece of music sounds really strange.

04:24.300 --> 04:25.670
Wait, Eleina,

04:25.960 --> 04:28.630
can you convert this song to image format?

04:28.630 --> 04:30.060
Let me try.

04:32.180 --> 04:33.350
This is...

04:33.680 --> 04:35.890
Hapna's clinical trial data.

04:36.350 --> 04:37.810
You can understand those?

04:38.520 --> 04:40.650
Yes, a little.

04:41.070 --> 04:42.190
Wait a minute.

04:42.480 --> 04:44.420
Why go through all the trouble to encode it

04:44.420 --> 04:46.360
and upload it to SNS?

04:46.360 --> 04:47.440
It's meant

04:47.570 --> 04:51.240
for people who want to hide their whereabouts.

04:51.580 --> 04:52.740
That means...

04:52.740 --> 04:54.040
Skinner!

04:54.290 --> 04:55.159
Great!

04:55.159 --> 04:57.330
Now we've got so much evidence.

04:57.659 --> 05:00.000
Let's go ask them directly.

05:09.050 --> 05:10.060
Huh?

05:10.060 --> 05:11.850
Wait, what?

05:15.640 --> 05:18.760
Rich people's security systems are on another level.

05:18.930 --> 05:20.110
I'm being jammed by their signals,

05:20.110 --> 05:21.610
and the drone can't get anywhere close.

05:21.610 --> 05:25.070
There's no nearby building to jump from either.

05:27.980 --> 05:29.980
The underground parking lot of the office building

05:29.980 --> 05:33.310
is fully automated and is not connected to other buildings.

05:33.830 --> 05:38.330
Then, how about landing from the rooftop?

05:38.330 --> 05:40.040
Of course, I won't be the one to do it.

05:40.040 --> 05:41.090
That's a good idea.

05:41.090 --> 05:42.630
Like Spider-Man.

05:42.630 --> 05:44.000
I want to try it.

05:44.000 --> 05:45.000
Wait, hold on.

05:45.000 --> 05:46.730
That'd be way too conspicuous.

05:46.880 --> 05:49.210
Let's wait until nightfall to make our move.

05:49.210 --> 05:51.100
What? Axel.

05:51.680 --> 05:52.930
What are you doing?

05:53.220 --> 05:54.680
Can you hear me?

05:54.890 --> 05:57.470
There are muscular guards everywhere.

06:09.310 --> 06:10.370
[Analyzing]

06:23.040 --> 06:24.330
Hi, hello.

06:25.040 --> 06:26.040
Hello.

06:28.170 --> 06:29.040
Who is that?

06:29.290 --> 06:30.470
I don't know.

07:04.710 --> 07:08.790
That guy... really charged in.

08:33.919 --> 08:35.510
Don't move.

08:36.010 --> 08:39.090
Can you shut down the entire security system?

08:39.590 --> 08:42.470
No. That's...

08:42.470 --> 08:44.560
Pretty please.

08:46.350 --> 08:49.600
Shut down the entire security system.

08:56.480 --> 08:57.570
Thank you.

08:59.820 --> 09:00.910
Who are you?

09:04.700 --> 09:06.870
How did you get these?

09:07.240 --> 09:08.830
Hi, Mr. CEO.

09:09.790 --> 09:13.250
This is the data you uploaded online, right?

09:15.000 --> 09:16.460
What do you want?

09:16.670 --> 09:17.500
Money?

09:17.500 --> 09:18.340
No.

09:18.840 --> 09:21.100
We want to know where Skinner is.

09:24.310 --> 09:28.060
No one wants to know that more than I do.

09:28.680 --> 09:33.070
He never told us his location or gave us any way to contact him.

09:33.650 --> 09:37.690
That's why I could only transmit data that way.

09:38.070 --> 09:39.920
Did you know that Hapna can suddenly mutate

09:39.920 --> 09:41.530
and become toxic?

09:41.530 --> 09:43.490
How could I have known that?

09:43.490 --> 09:45.950
What good would that do us if it's poisonous?

09:46.030 --> 09:48.760
Is there any concrete proof that Hapna is lethal?

09:49.660 --> 09:51.990
Before we entered human clinical trials,

09:52.040 --> 09:54.630
we experimented on monkeys.

09:55.630 --> 09:57.590
One of the monkeys

09:57.840 --> 09:59.790
died just a few days ago.

10:01.300 --> 10:02.850
I heard that its eyes

10:03.260 --> 10:06.470
had star-shaped spots like galaxies.

10:08.930 --> 10:11.440
Now it's our turn.

10:11.440 --> 10:14.310
Can't your company develop an antidote?

10:14.310 --> 10:17.980
The company's investing all its funds into that right now,

10:17.980 --> 10:20.870
but our entire research team is stumped.

10:21.240 --> 10:24.410
That man is simply a demon.

10:25.200 --> 10:26.990
If that guy is a demon,

10:27.320 --> 10:29.370
then us fighting him...

10:29.370 --> 10:32.210
that would make us angels, right?

10:33.040 --> 10:35.750
I'm tired of chasing after Skinner's ass.

10:36.710 --> 10:38.380
Let's lure him out.

10:40.840 --> 10:43.890
Delta Medicinal will hold an emergency press conference

10:43.890 --> 10:46.590
to announce a cure for Hapna.

10:46.890 --> 10:50.440
You've sent this to renowned scholars and relevant parties?

10:50.440 --> 10:51.350
Yes.

10:51.560 --> 10:55.100
If Skinner learns there's an antidote for the drug he created,

10:55.400 --> 10:57.660
he'll surely come in person to verify it.

10:57.900 --> 11:00.530
So you mean holding a fake press conference

11:00.530 --> 11:03.660
as a trap to catch him?

11:03.660 --> 11:04.950
That's the plan.

11:05.240 --> 11:07.780
There will be a hearing committee soon.

11:07.780 --> 11:08.860
You've heard about it, right?

11:08.860 --> 11:09.740
Yes.

11:09.740 --> 11:11.870
If we don't have results by then,

11:12.250 --> 11:15.110
the situation will become very unfavorable for us.

11:15.290 --> 11:16.460
Exactly.

11:17.290 --> 11:21.880
We can't afford to fail at this point.

11:22.510 --> 11:31.520
[LAZARUS]

11:32.140 --> 11:35.520
[Delta Medicinal]

11:33.060 --> 11:35.520
Will he really show up?

11:35.520 --> 11:38.810
At least he'll have his hacker connect to the site.

11:35.520 --> 11:38.810
[Delta]

11:38.810 --> 11:41.860
Maybe Skinner himself will show up.

11:41.860 --> 11:43.610
Not bad.

11:43.610 --> 11:46.030
I'll be waiting for you, Skinner baby.

11:47.360 --> 11:49.760
They really look just like real antidotes.

11:49.780 --> 11:52.910
Since there's a chance these ampoules might be stolen,

11:52.910 --> 11:55.750
each one contains a micro-GPS tracker.

11:56.370 --> 11:58.040
What's inside?

11:58.040 --> 11:59.660
Just saline solution.

12:00.840 --> 12:03.630
The question is what our enemy will do.

12:03.880 --> 12:06.300
Will they attack from the outside?

12:06.300 --> 12:07.550
Or...

12:07.550 --> 12:10.480
To try to sneak in disguised as guests?

12:11.020 --> 12:13.390
My exclusive security company

12:13.390 --> 12:16.600
has already swept the venue for bugs or other devices.

12:16.930 --> 12:18.810
Including myself, 50 people

12:18.810 --> 12:21.360
have set up tight security measures.

12:21.570 --> 12:24.610
All guards' backgrounds have been checked.

12:24.610 --> 12:27.900
Skinner's accomplices couldn't possibly sneak in.

12:28.320 --> 12:31.500
Luring him here with the press conference is a solid plan,

12:31.500 --> 12:33.450
but if he hacks into the internal network,

12:33.450 --> 12:35.410
he'll find out the antidote is fake.

12:35.410 --> 12:37.450
And that's where Eleina comes in.

12:37.870 --> 12:40.170
Delta Medicinal's internal network

12:40.170 --> 12:42.300
is largely divided into two sections:

12:42.380 --> 12:45.340
the core network, which handles confidential data,

12:45.340 --> 12:49.420
and the basic network, which manages building operations.

12:49.670 --> 12:51.520
What is this pattern?

12:51.680 --> 12:53.180
The core network.

12:53.180 --> 12:57.020
In other words, this room is entirely cut off from the rest of the network,

12:57.020 --> 12:58.770
and the walls are shielded.

12:58.770 --> 13:00.070
No signal can be connected.

12:58.810 --> 13:00.360
[Control Room]

13:00.190 --> 13:02.150
So, it's air-gapped?

13:00.360 --> 13:02.150
[Isolated]

13:02.360 --> 13:04.280
Mobile phones don't work in here either.

13:04.280 --> 13:06.780
If something happens, use this direct line.

13:07.030 --> 13:07.780
This way,

13:07.780 --> 13:10.370
invading the core network is simply impossible.

13:10.370 --> 13:12.290
Isn't that too difficult?

13:12.290 --> 13:15.370
If they give up, all of our efforts will be wasted.

13:15.370 --> 13:16.200
No.

13:16.700 --> 13:19.620
The more difficult it is, the more motivated they'll become.

13:19.620 --> 13:21.000
That's how hackers are.

13:22.630 --> 13:23.800
To bait them,

13:23.800 --> 13:27.090
we'll keep the basic network connected externally.

13:27.090 --> 13:30.060
That means you're planning to catch the hacker there, right?

13:30.060 --> 13:31.680
It's about time to start.

13:31.850 --> 13:33.350
Everyone, stay alert.

13:33.350 --> 13:35.100
Come on, Skinner.

13:35.310 --> 13:36.850
Let's play.

13:44.520 --> 13:46.110
All electronic devices

13:46.110 --> 13:48.690
must be left at the entrance.

14:00.380 --> 14:03.670
Sorry, there's one more.

14:05.340 --> 14:06.500
Who is that?

14:06.840 --> 14:08.090
Patrick Wong,

14:08.340 --> 14:09.790
Assistant Professor at MIT.

14:09.790 --> 14:11.510
What's his relationship with Skinner?

14:11.510 --> 14:15.220
He had a professor who used to be Skinner's colleague.

14:15.600 --> 14:17.350
We need to keep an eye on him.

14:25.360 --> 14:28.110
CEO, are you feeling alright?

14:28.110 --> 14:29.190
Yes.

14:29.190 --> 14:31.240
Sorry for making you worry.

14:31.620 --> 14:34.030
I once thought Skinner was a demon

14:34.030 --> 14:35.490
and felt despair.

14:35.820 --> 14:37.240
But I've been told

14:37.240 --> 14:40.880
that even against demons, you just need to stand and fight.

14:42.330 --> 14:44.880
I think they're right.

14:45.170 --> 14:47.920
I had forgotten that I could stand and fight.

14:48.960 --> 14:51.620
I actually slept well for the first time in ages.

14:53.550 --> 14:54.640
Ladies and gentlemen,

14:54.640 --> 14:57.050
sorry to keep you waiting.

14:57.340 --> 15:00.940
First, our CEO, Ahmed Rahman,

15:00.940 --> 15:02.980
will give an opening speech.

15:03.770 --> 15:05.810
Thank you all for coming today

15:05.810 --> 15:07.850
despite your busy schedules.

15:08.310 --> 15:11.410
Next, we will announce

15:11.410 --> 15:15.320
our successful development of a cure for Hapna.

15:15.950 --> 15:18.490
Now, Researcher Merrigan

15:18.490 --> 15:20.370
will explain to everyone.

15:21.040 --> 15:22.540
As you all know,

15:22.540 --> 15:25.000
Hapna's pain-relief mechanism

15:25.000 --> 15:30.340
involves the SCN9A gene, which regulates the sodium channel Nav1.7

15:30.340 --> 15:32.760
in Schwann cells.

15:33.880 --> 15:35.540
Someone went to the bathroom.

15:35.970 --> 15:37.130
Send someone to tail him.

15:37.130 --> 15:38.180
Roger.

15:39.260 --> 15:40.350
Coming.

15:41.060 --> 15:43.390
Someone is trying to access from outside.

15:44.770 --> 15:47.520
The access source is the Arctic.

15:47.520 --> 15:48.640
Military?

15:48.640 --> 15:50.360
No, it's a disguise.

15:50.360 --> 15:53.020
More incoming connections from other sources.

15:53.280 --> 15:55.820
It blocks sodium ion permeability,

15:55.820 --> 15:58.320
which causes creatures to die...

15:59.650 --> 16:01.250
What happened?

16:01.250 --> 16:02.160
What's wrong?

16:02.660 --> 16:03.460
What's wrong?

16:03.750 --> 16:04.550
Power outage?

16:04.620 --> 16:05.540
Eleina.

16:05.540 --> 16:08.540
This room has an independent power system. It's fine.

16:08.660 --> 16:09.750
This is...

16:09.960 --> 16:11.880
The network hasn't been hacked.

16:12.220 --> 16:13.510
What's going on?

16:13.510 --> 16:15.420
The earlier access attempt was a feint.

16:14.880 --> 16:18.340
[All Blocked]

16:15.800 --> 16:18.340
The perpetrator is inside this building.

16:18.760 --> 16:21.020
Someone, go check the main power supply.

16:21.140 --> 16:22.180
Roger.

16:23.390 --> 16:24.640
What about the man who went to the restroom?

16:24.640 --> 16:25.890
He hasn't come out yet.

16:25.890 --> 16:27.020
It's him.

16:27.020 --> 16:28.390
Seal off the entrance.

16:28.560 --> 16:29.770
Don't let anyone out!

16:29.770 --> 16:30.650
Understood!

16:30.650 --> 16:31.400
Chris,

16:31.400 --> 16:32.650
get inside!

16:32.650 --> 16:33.610
Okay.

16:41.080 --> 16:41.950
What?

16:42.250 --> 16:43.750
It's not this guy.

16:43.750 --> 16:45.950
Nothing wrong with the main power either.

16:45.950 --> 16:47.580
What's going on?

16:48.660 --> 16:49.660
Who's there?

16:58.420 --> 16:59.300
Great.

16:59.300 --> 17:01.350
Now I won't die.

17:02.430 --> 17:04.470
Detain the disruptor in a separate room

17:04.470 --> 17:05.770
and find out who he is.

17:07.470 --> 17:09.270
You can say whatever you want,

17:09.270 --> 17:13.230
but I'm not letting you hog the antidote!

17:13.440 --> 17:14.690
Mister,

17:14.690 --> 17:17.950
I'm sorry, but what you injected was just saline solution.

17:20.040 --> 17:21.790
This has nothing to do with Skinner either.

17:21.790 --> 17:25.079
Where is the attacker?

17:25.200 --> 17:28.540
Rewriting!

17:47.060 --> 17:49.100
Infinite loop rewriting.

17:49.100 --> 17:51.230
Just wrote a new program?

17:52.190 --> 17:53.820
Not bad.

17:56.270 --> 17:57.570
It's so hot.

17:58.110 --> 17:59.320
This is bad.

17:59.320 --> 18:01.120
The air conditioner is being controlled?

18:01.120 --> 18:02.450
Don't open the door.

18:06.410 --> 18:08.370
What's going on?

18:11.380 --> 18:13.090
Darn it.

18:16.670 --> 18:18.960
The core's been hacked.

18:19.210 --> 18:21.510
[Attacked]

18:19.380 --> 18:21.440
Hacked from 50 different locations.

18:21.760 --> 18:23.970
You mean there are 50 people hiding here?

18:23.970 --> 18:24.970
Seriously?

18:25.760 --> 18:27.220
Not 50 people.

18:28.390 --> 18:29.390
It's 50 devices.

18:29.720 --> 18:31.150
The security guards' radios.

18:31.150 --> 18:33.480
They used those to hack in!

18:33.810 --> 18:36.360
Can this communicate externally?

18:36.360 --> 18:39.110
No, it doesn't have that function.

18:39.110 --> 18:40.320
It's just a radio.

18:40.320 --> 18:42.530
And these units have just been replaced with new models.

18:42.530 --> 18:43.700
Replaced with new ones?

18:43.700 --> 18:45.990
The manufacturer contacted us about recalling the products

18:45.990 --> 18:47.240
and sent new ones.

18:47.240 --> 18:48.370
That's it.

18:48.370 --> 18:50.040
The attacker's plan all along

18:50.040 --> 18:53.640
was to have the guards bring these devices into the control room.

18:53.710 --> 18:54.630
What should we do?

18:54.630 --> 18:57.230
If the core is hacked, our plan will be exposed.

18:57.880 --> 18:59.000
Eleina.

19:03.930 --> 19:05.260
They've taken the bait.

19:06.590 --> 19:07.890
Starting to track.

19:07.890 --> 19:08.970
[Silver Bullet]

19:10.060 --> 19:11.190
I anticipated this,

19:11.190 --> 19:12.430
so I planted fake Hapna data

19:12.430 --> 19:14.690
on the core network server.

19:14.690 --> 19:17.690
Now we can pinpoint Popcorn Wizard's location.

19:14.690 --> 19:17.690
[Silver Bullet]

19:17.900 --> 19:21.110
Deliberately sacrificing a part to take down the hacker, right?

19:21.110 --> 19:23.320
The cost is that they'll gain control of the core network.

19:23.320 --> 19:24.520
So we must be careful.

19:24.950 --> 19:26.700
[No Future]

19:28.360 --> 19:29.450
Hold on!

19:31.250 --> 19:32.580
What's with these?

19:34.210 --> 19:35.920
What should we do?

19:36.460 --> 19:38.080
Try to hold on somehow!

19:38.370 --> 19:39.540
Got it.

19:41.590 --> 19:42.760
In Pakistan,

19:42.760 --> 19:45.010
the Islamabad Stock Exchange.

19:45.340 --> 19:48.090
I'll request the local police to take action.

19:48.840 --> 19:53.270
Stock exchanges everywhere have first-rate infrastructure.

19:53.770 --> 19:55.440
By hijacking their connections,

19:55.440 --> 19:59.040
one can process large volumes of communication traffic, right?

20:07.900 --> 20:09.150
Can't find the person?

20:09.150 --> 20:10.210
What's happening?

20:11.750 --> 20:13.330
They're moving.

20:13.750 --> 20:15.370
In a remote mountain area like this,

20:15.370 --> 20:17.370
with such large traffic volumes...

20:17.540 --> 20:18.500
Could it be...

20:30.890 --> 20:34.270
All right, let's take a look at the antidote.

20:36.560 --> 20:38.680
Pretty vacant!

20:38.680 --> 20:41.820
The antidote is indeed fake.

20:43.570 --> 20:45.400
Not bad.

20:51.160 --> 20:52.250
What's wrong?

20:52.250 --> 20:53.870
It's over.

20:55.160 --> 20:56.790
They got away.

20:57.700 --> 20:59.950
Probably to confuse us,

20:59.950 --> 21:03.880
they specifically set up a mobile base near the stock exchange.

21:06.260 --> 21:09.300
Not only did we make sacrifices, but we got played.

21:09.630 --> 21:11.020
I'm sorry.

21:11.220 --> 21:12.560
What now?

21:18.060 --> 21:20.190
Popcorn Wizard.

21:20.440 --> 21:21.530
Himself, for real?

21:21.530 --> 21:22.650
No way.

21:23.940 --> 21:25.730
Not bad!

21:26.650 --> 21:29.900
Well played, pretty vacant.

21:29.900 --> 21:31.950
You're the first one

21:31.950 --> 21:33.830
to push me this far.

21:35.410 --> 21:36.240
Well...

21:36.240 --> 21:39.240
Johnny Rotten is my hero.

21:39.240 --> 21:40.840
Goodbye, bye!

21:41.250 --> 21:42.880
Wait, Popcorn!

21:44.710 --> 21:46.210
She hung up.

22:06.520 --> 22:10.580
Not bad!

22:15.490 --> 22:18.740
[21 Days Left...]

22:40.980 --> 22:47.400
♪ I, I must being losing my mind ♪

22:48.900 --> 22:53.910
♪ I keep on trying to find a way out ♪

22:53.910 --> 23:00.500
♪ But there is no need, don't lock the door anymore ♪

23:04.130 --> 23:10.470
♪ I, you know I never go out ♪

23:12.510 --> 23:16.970
♪ And you know I start to forgetting things ♪

23:16.970 --> 23:18.800
